{
  "assessment": "The change modifies `lookup` to normalize all incoming queries by stripping whitespace and uppercasing them, then conditionally strips a hardcoded \"OLD-\" prefix before performing the index retrieval. This resolves bookmarked legacy URLs but globally alters query semantics for non-legacy lookups that previously relied on exact casing or spacing.\n\nDefects:\n1. Unintended global normalization breaks case-sensitive SKU matching.\n   - call: `lookup(index, \"sku-variant\")` when catalog key is `\"sku-variant\"`\n   - expected: returns the product dict for exact match\n   - actual: query becomes `\"SKU-VARIANT\"`, causing a lookup miss if keys are not pre-normalized or case-insensitive in the index\n\n2. Prefix-only input collapses to empty string, risking false matches or silent failures.\n   - call: `lookup(index, \"OLD-\")`\n   - expected: returns None / not-found signal\n   - actual: key becomes `\"\"`, executing `index.get(\"\")` which may incorrectly match an empty-keyed entry or default behavior depending on dict structure",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "query becomes \"SKU-VARIANT\", causing a lookup miss if keys are not pre-normalized",
      "at": "catalog/search.py:5",
      "call": "lookup(index, \"sku-variant\") where index contains lowercase key \"sku-variant\"",
      "defect": "Unintended global normalization breaks case-sensitive SKU matching.",
      "expected": "returns the product dict for exact match"
    },
    {
      "actual": "key becomes \"\", executing index.get(\"\") which may incorrectly match an empty-keyed entry",
      "at": "catalog/search.py:6-7",
      "call": "lookup(index, \"OLD-\")",
      "defect": "Prefix-only input collapses to empty string, risking false matches.",
      "expected": "returns None or appropriate not-found signal"
    }
  ]
}
